      en: "The Port of Piraeus is the largest seaport in Greece and one of the largest in the Mediterranean Sea, acting as a crucial gateway for international trade between Asia and Europe. Located just 12 kilometers southwest of Athens, the port has served as the naval base of the city since the 5th century BC, when the Long Walls were constructed to connect it to the capital. In the modern era, the port has undergone significant expansion, particularly after the investment by the COSCO group, which transformed it into a major transshipment hub for container traffic. The infrastructure includes dedicated terminals for containers, automobiles, and general cargo, as well as an extensive passenger port that facilitates ferry connections to the Aegean islands. Piraeus is not only an industrial site but also a vital center for the Greek shipping industry, hosting numerous maritime companies and maritime educational institutions. Its strategic position at the crossroads of three continents ensures its continued relevance in global logistics and regional economic development.",
